--- body ---
## Context

Round 2 of the Imperial Dragon skill renames (0067/0068, PR #304).
Author decisions, 2026-06-05:

- `verify` → `gaze` (the dragon's gaze as the verification ward).
  `review-pr` keeps its name — never invoked by hand, it is plumbing
  called by `/verify`. Bonus: renaming IDH `verify` removes the name
  collision with Claude Code's built-in `verify` skill.
- `start-ticket` → `hunt` — pairs semantically with `raid`.
- `check-readiness` → `scry`, `housekeeping` → `molt` — approved, but
  discoverability and memorability will take a while: **aliases are
  musts**. The descriptive names stay as permanent aliases, not
  deprecation stubs.
- `perch` stays (`coil` rejected).

## Mechanism

Same stub pattern as 0067: old-name `SKILL.md` delegates to the new
canonical via the Skill tool (Claude Code has no native alias
mechanism — command name = directory name). Two framings:

- `verify`, `start-ticket`: deprecation stubs as in 0067 (warn line,
  e.g. "Skill verify renamed gaze. Gazing.", then delegate).
- `check-readiness`, `housekeeping`: permanent alias stubs — no
  deprecated language; catalog description keeps the descriptive
  text prefixed "Alias of /scry —" / "Alias of /molt —".

## Actions

1. `git mv` each skill dir to its dragon name; update frontmatter
   `name:`, self-references, and helper-script paths.
2. Write the four old-name stubs (framings above),
   `disable-model-invocation: true`.
3. Call-site sweep — `verify` especially is invoked from `raid`,
   `beat`, `nightbeat-supervisor`, `reviewers`, rules, scripts and
   tests. `verify-gate` and `verify-adherence` keep their names
   (plumbing called by gaze). Stubs keep any missed call site
   working, but sweep anyway.
4. `make skills-catalog`; update README prose if needed.
5. Run `make check`, pytest, `erg check`.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `skills/gaze/`, `skills/hunt/`, `skills/scry/`, `skills/molt/` exist with full content
- [x] Old names resolve via stubs: verify/start-ticket warn-and-delegate; check-readiness/housekeeping silently alias
- [x] No un-swept old-name references in skills/, rules/, scripts/, tests/ (excluding the stubs themselves and closed tickets)
- [x] `make check` + pytest pass; catalog in sync
